WEBVTT

00:01.500 --> 00:04.230
<b>Kawakamimaru</b>

00:09.980 --> 00:11.510
<b>Shiriuchi River
Toppu River
Sorachi River
Saru River</b>

00:11.510 --> 00:13.610
<b>Lake Shikotsu
Pirate</b>

00:12.360 --> 00:16.990
Oh? They were looking for me?

00:55.920 --> 01:04.660
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

01:47.730 --> 01:52.560
<b>Episode Forty-Eight
Discharge</b>

01:48.030 --> 01:50.890
From the way Botaro the Pirate was talking,

01:50.890 --> 01:55.920
he may already know where 
the Ainu first hid the gold.

01:55.920 --> 02:00.130
But he also said that's not 
enough to find it on its own.

02:00.440 --> 02:05.440
What do you think about the rumors 
that the tattooed skins are worthless?

02:06.300 --> 02:12.130
I think we should ignore it and 
keep looking for the skins.

02:12.130 --> 02:16.690
Well, for now, let's pretend to work 
with him and get information, okay?

02:25.570 --> 02:28.850
We're at our last stop, Ebetsu Port.

02:28.850 --> 02:32.390
I suppose being one of my 
citizens isn't enough for you.

02:35.100 --> 02:38.700
How much gold did you hear about being there?

02:39.050 --> 02:40.380
Twenty kan, right?

02:40.610 --> 02:42.810
They filled deerskin bags about this 
big until they were overstuffed,

02:42.810 --> 02:46.160
according to what the old Ainu men said.

02:46.160 --> 02:48.680
One bag was about 16 kan,

02:48.680 --> 02:50.950
and there were over 1,200 of them.

02:50.950 --> 02:53.500
A whole mountain of the stuff.

03:01.070 --> 03:02.130
Well?

03:02.130 --> 03:03.570
Quite a story, right?

03:04.390 --> 03:07.080
I'm sorry we won't be able 
to chase the dream together.

03:14.710 --> 03:16.340
He saw inside our backpack!

03:21.090 --> 03:22.840
Yah!

03:22.840 --> 03:25.680
<b>Kawakamimaru</b>

03:46.120 --> 03:48.330
Gondo!

04:25.740 --> 04:26.950
Let me go!

04:44.590 --> 04:46.390
<b>Kawakamimaru</b>

04:44.810 --> 04:46.390
Asirpa-chan, can you swim?

04:46.640 --> 04:47.550
If it's not too deep!

04:47.550 --> 04:48.930
Then stay there!

05:29.210 --> 05:30.700
Pisikorkamuychep!

05:31.930 --> 05:33.180
Those are yupe!

05:53.540 --> 05:56.040
<b>Kawakamimaru</b>

05:54.580 --> 05:56.040
Sugimoto!

06:06.800 --> 06:08.660
<i>At the time, it was said sturgeons</i>

06:08.660 --> 06:11.560
<i>would travel upriver in the 
Ishikari River in huge schools.</i>

06:11.560 --> 06:14.970
<i>One theory says that the name "Ebetsu" 
came from the Ainu words "yupe ot,"</i>

06:15.210 --> 06:19.040
<i>or "there are many sturgeons."</i>

06:21.350 --> 06:24.980
The paddle wheel's damaged. I can't dock.

06:24.980 --> 06:27.400
I can't even move until another 
ship with a paddle wheel arrives.

06:27.400 --> 06:29.670
Sorry, Captain.

06:32.300 --> 06:35.660
My ship's a mess thanks to you assholes.

06:35.940 --> 06:37.470
Get lost!

06:37.470 --> 06:40.490
Sugimoto, the platinum that Heita had...

06:40.490 --> 06:42.360
Yeah, you're right.

06:42.360 --> 06:43.420
Now...

06:45.470 --> 06:47.260
We're going to work together 
with Botaro the Pirate.

06:48.880 --> 06:51.880
You saved me because you wanted 
the information I have?

06:51.880 --> 06:55.780
You heard what Boss Wakayama 
said and changed your plans?

06:55.780 --> 06:59.480
No, we're still going 
to search for the skins.

06:59.790 --> 07:02.580
So you want me to help find the prisoners?

07:02.890 --> 07:06.110
I told you, I don't expect the 
code to ever be cracked.

07:06.110 --> 07:10.480
What that yakuza boss told you...
 It makes sense.

07:10.800 --> 07:15.700
But right now there are two main groups 
that have the vast majority of the skins.

07:16.000 --> 07:18.470
Hijikata Toshizou and Lieutenant Tsurumi...

07:18.920 --> 07:20.650
We can't ignore the fact that

07:20.650 --> 07:25.080
two people as intelligent and cunning 
as them are still looking for the skins.

07:25.850 --> 07:26.840
Good point!

07:26.840 --> 07:32.050
So you just want somebody else around 
who can help you steal the skins?

07:32.700 --> 07:39.370
Sugimoto, don't tell me you felt 
sympathy for Botaro, right?

07:40.690 --> 07:47.120
My intuition tells me that if he has 
found the region where the gold's hidden,

07:47.120 --> 07:53.690
that may be the one way to turn the tables 
on Hijikata Toshizou and Lieutenant Tsurumi.

07:54.560 --> 07:57.960
One option would be to torture him 
into telling us what we want to know.

07:57.960 --> 08:01.580
But any information we gained 
that way wouldn't be trustworthy.

08:01.580 --> 08:03.240
Which means we have no choice 
but to work together.

08:04.690 --> 08:06.270
I see.

08:07.630 --> 08:13.420
But you actually saved me 'cause you've 
taken a liking to me, right, Sugimoto?

08:16.620 --> 08:17.550
Fine.

08:18.200 --> 08:22.190
I'll give you the information 
I've got once you have the skins.

08:22.190 --> 08:23.970
For my own protection.

08:27.450 --> 08:29.880
I hope you don't regret this, Sugimoto.

08:30.200 --> 08:33.670
He might try to take all 
the gold when we find it.

08:33.670 --> 08:35.350
Are you talking about yourself?

08:37.520 --> 08:40.010
Oh, Mister Hood came down the river!

08:46.790 --> 08:50.010
We'll go down the river a little 
more before heading to Sapporo.

08:50.010 --> 08:52.070
Asirpa-san, what are you doing?

08:53.010 --> 08:53.830
That.

08:53.830 --> 08:56.760
Oh, I'm adding a "kite" to 
a rod I found on the ship.

08:57.530 --> 09:02.020
We always just carry the tip 
and use a stick we find nearby.

09:02.020 --> 09:04.060
The one you used for the whale?

09:04.060 --> 09:04.800
Yes.

09:04.800 --> 09:06.070
I'm surprised you remembered.

09:06.070 --> 09:07.770
You're gonna hunt sturgeons?

09:08.560 --> 09:11.960
Well, Sugimoto, you want to eat 
a seasonal delicacy, right?

09:11.960 --> 09:13.720
Well... yes.

09:14.090 --> 09:16.700
What's your relationship with this girl?

09:16.700 --> 09:19.210
She's my guide. For Hokkaido.

09:20.690 --> 09:23.290
But you got really mad back there!

09:23.500 --> 09:26.080
That put Asirpa-san in danger, shithead!

09:26.400 --> 09:28.960
I thought she was somebody 
who meant a lot to you.

09:36.400 --> 09:38.180
Look at all these fish eggs!

09:38.740 --> 09:41.170
We ate them pickled in salt 
when we were in Russia.

09:41.170 --> 09:43.140
They're all stuffed into its belly like this?

09:43.450 --> 09:46.950
You usually eat the meat of a yupe raw.

09:46.950 --> 09:51.020
Sometimes you'll make a stew with 
these black eggs and its other parts.

09:51.770 --> 09:53.740
Of course, you eat the brains, too!

09:53.740 --> 09:57.690
I'd love to feed them to you now, but the 
skull's really hard, so give me a minute.

09:57.690 --> 10:00.160
Sorry, Sugimoto! I'm sorry!

10:00.780 --> 10:02.810
I'll feed you really soon, okay?

10:00.780 --> 10:03.680
Aw, hurry up, okay?

10:10.430 --> 10:13.510
Asirpa-chan, do you like sturgeon brains?

10:14.230 --> 10:16.640
I like all types of animal brains.

10:16.640 --> 10:19.050
They taste good salted.

10:19.290 --> 10:23.470
When you like someone, you want them 
to like the things you like, right?

10:24.560 --> 10:26.070
You talk too much.

10:26.070 --> 10:27.290
Eat some black fish eggs and shut up.

10:30.690 --> 10:32.520
Do you have a family, Asirpa-chan?

10:32.520 --> 10:34.750
I have Huci... my grandmother.

10:34.750 --> 10:36.280
Just your grandmother?

10:36.730 --> 10:40.070
It feels like you've been traveling 
with the three of them for a long time.

10:40.070 --> 10:42.520
You don't think she's worried 
about her granddaughter?

10:43.300 --> 10:46.290
It'll be dangerous to stay with us.
 Why don't you go home?

10:53.050 --> 10:55.000
You want to stay with them no matter what?

10:55.330 --> 10:59.120
It tastes so much better fresh than salted!

10:59.120 --> 11:02.170
Sturgeon eggs go really well with vodka...

11:02.170 --> 11:05.930
It washes away that fishy aftertaste.

11:06.260 --> 11:09.320
I'm not here because I want to be with them.

11:11.210 --> 11:12.490
That's not why.

11:13.810 --> 11:17.450
I've got something I have to do. 
So I don't care about anything else.

11:19.280 --> 11:22.950
This is an ohaw made from black 
eggs and pisikorkamuychep filet.

11:23.560 --> 11:25.380
Here you go, Sugimoto! The brains!

11:28.240 --> 11:30.270
Hinna, hinna, hinna!

11:30.270 --> 11:32.370
What are you doing?

11:32.370 --> 11:35.880
<b>Otaru</b>

11:46.350 --> 11:47.850
Khorosho!

12:05.140 --> 12:10.040
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

12:10.040 --> 12:12.500
<b>Sapporo</b>

12:13.160 --> 12:15.140
Private Usami,

12:15.140 --> 12:19.460
your theory that the killer will return to 
the scene of the crime sounds plausible.

12:19.810 --> 12:22.350
But are you planning on 
waiting for him all day

12:22.350 --> 12:24.630
when we have no idea when he'll come back?

12:25.060 --> 12:27.210
There are two murder sites.

12:27.210 --> 12:30.570
Wouldn't we be better off asking the whores?

12:30.930 --> 12:34.190
Fapfapfapfapfapfap!

12:32.020 --> 12:33.020
Usami?!

12:34.190 --> 12:36.110
No, it's not here.

12:36.110 --> 12:37.080
Here?

12:37.080 --> 12:39.470
No, closer to here?

12:39.860 --> 12:40.640
Hey!

12:40.640 --> 12:42.150
Be quiet!

12:42.150 --> 12:43.680
Don't talk to me right now!

12:44.950 --> 12:45.920
Here!

12:46.250 --> 12:48.350
This position, facing this way, 
is where I feel most calm.

12:48.350 --> 12:49.580
It feels right.

12:49.580 --> 12:51.980
Nobody could see me from 
the surrounding buildings,

12:51.980 --> 12:54.130
and it's hidden from the road!

12:54.130 --> 12:57.500
I can run away and be sure 
that nobody will see my face!

13:02.220 --> 13:04.060
Neigh-hay!

13:06.270 --> 13:07.610
Neigh-hay?

13:08.720 --> 13:11.370
Where? Where did it fall?

13:11.370 --> 13:13.480
Usami, your clothes will get dirty.

13:18.130 --> 13:19.150
Found it.

13:19.780 --> 13:22.420
I found it, Warrant Officer Kikuta.

13:22.420 --> 13:23.860
This way.

13:24.210 --> 13:26.790
What? I don't want to look at your sperm.

13:26.790 --> 13:27.910
Talk about gross.

13:27.910 --> 13:29.840
No, it's the killer's.

13:29.840 --> 13:32.330
The killer did come back.

13:32.330 --> 13:34.370
And he was masturbating, too!

13:35.370 --> 13:36.970
From the state of these clumps...

13:36.970 --> 13:39.710
Don't touch it! You'll get a disease, Usami!

13:41.540 --> 13:43.640
He comes once every two days.

13:43.640 --> 13:46.120
And the last time he came was two days ago.

13:47.320 --> 13:49.550
He'll arrive tonight.

13:49.790 --> 13:51.500
I can't believe what I'm seeing.

13:51.500 --> 13:53.930
You're a sperm detective.

13:54.150 --> 13:56.710
What Lieutenant Tsurumi said...

13:56.710 --> 14:00.100
I'm sure Usami will be useful in Sapporo.

14:00.100 --> 14:02.110
Is this what he meant?

14:02.110 --> 14:04.520
I'll try again.

14:04.920 --> 14:06.900
This time, I might be able 
to figure out their age

14:06.900 --> 14:10.080
and how tall they are from 
the distance and height!

14:10.080 --> 14:12.910
I didn't know you had a 
special power like that...

14:14.470 --> 14:17.690
Fapfapfapfapfapfap...

14:17.690 --> 14:19.040
Fapfapfapfapfapfap...

14:25.050 --> 14:26.380
What the hell?

14:26.380 --> 14:28.250
This is the killer!

14:38.680 --> 14:40.350
What the hell is this?!

14:45.180 --> 14:46.280
Usami, you go that way!

15:20.140 --> 15:21.450
Gotcha!

15:22.400 --> 15:24.610
Fapfapfapfapfapfap...

15:32.240 --> 15:35.100
Are you okay, Warrant Officer Kikuta?

15:36.350 --> 15:38.370
It got in my eyes!

15:54.390 --> 15:56.330
Did he do that?

15:56.330 --> 15:58.310
While running from us?

16:00.700 --> 16:03.870
Good evening, good evening...

16:04.690 --> 16:08.610
Where are you heading in 
such a hurry, Mister Foreigner?

16:20.300 --> 16:23.440
I forgive your sins.

16:23.440 --> 16:25.580
Excellent... Excellent...

16:33.970 --> 16:36.220
He killed two in a night.

16:36.450 --> 16:38.850
Maybe it was his way of covering his escape.

16:38.850 --> 16:41.660
Or maybe he was just trying to screw with us.

16:41.660 --> 16:43.350
It's possible that we had 
nothing to do with it.

16:43.600 --> 16:46.880
He'd already decided to kill.

16:46.880 --> 16:48.820
Will he come back?

16:49.280 --> 16:53.450
It'll be hard for the two of us to do 
a stakeout when there are four places.

16:53.670 --> 16:56.990
And he might make more holy places for himself.

16:56.990 --> 16:58.450
Holy places?

16:58.880 --> 17:03.660
We let the bastard get away, but I did
 get a good look at his face.

17:03.660 --> 17:05.990
And the mark on his dick.

17:07.630 --> 17:10.050
Let's go see the other body.

17:10.050 --> 17:11.840
There's a big crowd gathered around it.

17:12.100 --> 17:14.070
There might be somebody we saw yesterday.

17:14.070 --> 17:15.440
Go on ahead.

17:15.440 --> 17:16.770
I need to take a piss.

17:22.680 --> 17:24.430
Private Ariko Rikimatsu.

17:28.440 --> 17:29.680
Don't turn around.

17:32.180 --> 17:36.110
Did you think I wouldn't recognize your 
figure after I've seen it a billion times?

17:36.110 --> 17:40.250
Lieutenant Tsurumi didn't say anything 
about you being in Sapporo.

17:40.800 --> 17:42.580
You with Hijikata Toshizou?

17:42.790 --> 17:45.200
I've had somebody around me at all times.

17:45.200 --> 17:48.080
That's why I haven't been able 
to report to Lieutenant Tsurumi.

17:48.650 --> 17:51.000
We can't let anyone see us like this.

17:51.000 --> 17:53.840
I was just with Nagakura Shinpachi.

17:54.130 --> 17:56.970
Hijikata Toshizou's men suspect me.

17:57.530 --> 17:59.390
And Lieutenant Tsurumi, too...

17:59.390 --> 18:01.970
Nobody trusts me.

18:02.570 --> 18:04.100
Then work for me.

18:06.010 --> 18:08.190
Listen carefully to me, Ariko.

18:08.430 --> 18:10.950
I'm the only one who believes you.

18:10.950 --> 18:13.320
Forget what your Ainu dad wanted.

18:13.680 --> 18:17.200
Forget about your relations 
that Lieutenant Tsurumi threatened.

18:17.510 --> 18:20.200
Following either one of them will 
only lead you to destruction.

18:20.580 --> 18:25.580
The government told me to have Lieutenant 
Tsurumi find the gold, and then kill him.

18:26.000 --> 18:29.330
You're a spy for the government?

18:36.740 --> 18:40.010
I am your child.

18:42.540 --> 18:45.100
Papers! Get your newspapers here!

18:45.100 --> 18:48.980
Goldfish! Goldfish!

18:48.980 --> 18:55.030
When the goldfish seller comes to town, 
it feels like spring's really here.

18:55.030 --> 18:57.360
Goldfish!

18:57.360 --> 19:01.200
Fireworks! Fireworks!

19:09.440 --> 19:13.290
You make a particularly scary komusou monk, 
Ushiyama-san. You're hard to miss.

19:13.290 --> 19:15.390
I can't hide my muscles.

19:17.090 --> 19:20.880
Yeah, it's not good to disguise 
yourself as something that stands out.

19:20.880 --> 19:23.430
What the hell are you 
supposed to be, Kadokura?

19:32.820 --> 19:36.150
Yeah, you do stand out a little too much.

19:36.360 --> 19:39.390
It seems there's been a new 
development in the case.

19:39.390 --> 19:43.240
The bastard sent a letter to the papers.

19:43.520 --> 19:46.600
Inside was a human kidney.

19:46.600 --> 19:50.800
The fourth victim had their right kidney taken.

19:50.800 --> 19:52.730
What a lunatic.

19:52.730 --> 19:59.400
There was a letter attached 
which was barely legible.

19:59.400 --> 20:02.090
It read "whores are sinners" 
in a terrible scrawl,

20:02.090 --> 20:05.180
and swore that "I will kill again."

20:05.180 --> 20:08.000
And that's when I realized...

20:08.000 --> 20:11.060
This is a copycat of Jack the Ripper.

20:11.060 --> 20:12.260
Who?

20:12.260 --> 20:13.980
Jack the Ripper is said to be

20:13.980 --> 20:19.670
the man behind a series of famous 
serial killings in London.

20:19.670 --> 20:23.750
It had all of England in an uproar.

20:23.750 --> 20:30.620
In 1888, it was reported by several papers 
in Japan, too. It was quite the big story.

20:30.620 --> 20:37.240
The way those prostitutes died... 
Even the stolen organ, it's all the same.

20:37.240 --> 20:38.630
And that's not all.

20:39.720 --> 20:42.760
The other thing that made it 
such a huge deal in England

20:42.760 --> 20:52.520
<b>Hokkai Times</b>

20:43.060 --> 20:45.250
was that the killer sent 
a letter to the papers

20:45.250 --> 20:49.050
mocking the police and 
saying he would kill again.

20:49.050 --> 20:52.520
This was a totally new thing at the time.

20:52.920 --> 20:57.930
There were also hundreds of similar letters 
sent by copycats with no creativity.

20:57.930 --> 21:01.550
There were a number of prostitutes 
murdered around the same time,

21:01.550 --> 21:04.780
but only five were recognized 
as Jack's handiwork.

21:05.290 --> 21:09.360
He started killing women at intervals around 
one month apart after the first victim.

21:09.360 --> 21:13.230
The third and fourth were 
both slain the same night.

21:13.230 --> 21:18.090
The Sapporo murders follow 
this pattern exactly.

21:18.090 --> 21:22.960
He's probably not a copycat, but some 
kind of Jack the Ripper fanatic.

21:23.550 --> 21:26.990
The other thing that made the 
Jack the Ripper case famous

21:26.990 --> 21:30.560
was that the killer just disappeared.

21:31.090 --> 21:35.880
The last murder was performed 
40 days after the fourth.

21:35.880 --> 21:39.190
It's said the fifth murder is the last.

21:39.480 --> 21:47.530
So there's a chance the killer will simply 
disappear if we can't find him in 40 days?

21:47.530 --> 21:49.910
We have to find him and make him pay!

21:50.420 --> 21:53.290
I guess even the famous 
Ishikawa Takuboku is mad, huh?

21:53.290 --> 21:57.540
My favorite prostitute got
 scared and fled to Tokyo!

21:57.540 --> 21:59.910
Catch him as soon as you can!

21:59.910 --> 22:02.040
I want to bring her back to Sapporo!

22:02.040 --> 22:04.710
You're a piece of shit.

22:05.320 --> 22:09.550
There's also another incident 
that interests me...

22:09.900 --> 22:12.550
Hey, Sugimoto, you see this article?

22:12.550 --> 22:15.220
The one about another prostitute 
being killed in Sapporo?

22:15.220 --> 22:17.290
No, not that one.

22:17.290 --> 22:20.150
The one about the kids who keep 
disappearing from different locations.

22:20.150 --> 22:23.420
The most recent is three missing in Ebetsu.

22:23.420 --> 22:25.280
We were just there!

22:25.660 --> 22:28.640
A child kidnapper? It might be him.

22:28.640 --> 22:29.780
You know who it is?

22:30.110 --> 22:32.050
His name is Ueji Keiji.

22:32.050 --> 22:35.910
He's a murderer who buried 
many kids in his yard.

22:35.910 --> 22:39.540
A weird guy with tattoos that looked 
like a child's scribbles on his face.

22:39.540 --> 22:40.730
The candy peddler!

22:43.770 --> 22:48.600
Ueji Keiji is, of course, 
one of the tattooed prisoners.

22:49.860 --> 22:54.360
There's been a lot of children 
going missing from Hokkaido lately.

22:54.360 --> 23:01.570
It's happened recently in Asahikawa, 
Utashinai, Iwamizawa...

22:56.640 --> 23:02.770
<b>Sapporo</b>

22:56.640 --> 23:02.770
<b>Asahikawa</b>

22:59.100 --> 23:02.770
<b>Utashinai</b>

22:59.890 --> 23:02.770
<b>Iwamizawa</b>

23:01.570 --> 23:02.790
And Ebetsu.

23:01.600 --> 23:02.770
<b>Ebetsu</b>

23:02.790 --> 23:05.190
They're getting closer to Sapporo!

23:07.210 --> 23:10.740
What's about to happen in Sapporo?

23:10.740 --> 23:13.530
<b>Coast
of the
Okhotsk
 Sea</b>

23:11.530 --> 23:14.910
We got a telegram from 
Warrant Officer Kikuta.

23:14.910 --> 23:18.180
Two of you are to stay here and hunt Asirpa.

23:18.180 --> 23:21.190
The others are all to follow me.

23:21.190 --> 23:23.280
We're heading to Sapporo!

23:28.230 --> 23:30.670
I'm a son who loves his father very much.

23:31.070 --> 23:32.880
Please give donations.

23:32.880 --> 23:35.050
We're leaving, Ogata.

23:35.120 --> 23:40.250
<b>Next Time
The Vanished Kamuy</b>

23:35.570 --> 23:38.730
Next time: "The Vanished Kamuy"!
